[0m[0m
[1mOne real divergence found and fixed.[22m In [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m's [38;5;10mstrchr[0m reimplementation, the plain [38;5;10m*s[0m dereference made rustc insert a null-pointer check whenever debug assertions were on. For [38;5;10mfoo(NULL, 'A')[0m and [38;5;10mdriver(NULL)[0m the C [38;5;10m.so[0m dies with [38;5;10mSIGSEGV[0m (11) while the debug-built Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m died with [38;5;10mSIGABRT[0m (6) plus a message on stderr. Release passed because the check is compiled out — a profile-dependent behavior difference that only the out-of-process signal comparison could see. Switching the load to [38;5;10mcore::ptr::read_volatile(s)[0m issues the same byte load with no inserted check; fault parity now holds in debug, release, and release with [38;5;10m-Cdebug-assertions=on[0m forced.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mNotable finding while deriving the artifacts:[22m [38;5;10mfoo(in, '\0')[0m does not return 0 as one might assume. [38;5;10mstrchr(s, 0)[0m always matches a terminator, so it can never produce the NULL sentinel the [38;5;10mfor[0m loop relies on — the pointer walks out of the object indefinitely until the process faults. I established this empirically against the built C [38;5;10m.so[0m before recording it, and both libraries are confirmed to die by [38;5;10mSIGSEGV[0m identically. This is also what a full-width [38;5;10mint[0m needle whose low byte is zero (e.g. [38;5;10m0x100[0m, [38;5;10mINT_MIN[0m) does, which is covered as the out-of-range-value-across-FFI case.[0m[0m
